[{:db/id "q-79333/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "e2982eb2-2159-59db-9ba1-3b0538fe51a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79333/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8969a8b6-7e3b-5c4d-b05f-c8c253f7596e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79333/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "34c1ba00-0e56-5150-9cab-44a2b3259f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79333/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "84d06fc0-4ed4-560c-8333-af3559a8f046" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79333/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1ceb600f-0104-52b3-ab17-027a337a6cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79333/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3db0b1ef-c8dc-580f-8d9d-3d36b51250fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79333/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-79333/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-79333/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-79333/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-79333/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-79333/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79333" :question/id #uuid "026a0cae-bdc3-5eb5-888c-83ba0c1115ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-79333" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\frac{7}{x}$\n- $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$\n- $y=\\frac{2}{x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{7}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{7}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\frac{1}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{x})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{2}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{2}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{2}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79333/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "fc6b3f5c-d6da-5869-963a-d587df226830" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2e86f126-5240-5cb2-b281-3d3521c0921f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "19de3e4b-1afd-5bdb-9c4d-2e62671615a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "2e143d2f-ee04-5895-b088-8261f80d40f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d36bb8a4-5040-5b18-9dd1-e0abab000047" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d9dfc3b-5a30-52b4-9822-c3c4b31eb052" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141091/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-141091/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141091/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-141091/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141091/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-141091/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141091" :question/id #uuid "a471fc2f-d62d-516e-bc45-9db90390f695" :question/math-academy-id "q-141091" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1$\n- $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 0 & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141091/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141091"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-141096"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$\n- $y=-2{e}^{x}$\n- $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{-2x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{-2x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{-2x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{x}) \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 6{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2{e}^{-x}+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(2{e}^{-x}+1) \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-4{e}^{-x}-2 \\\\ 2{e}^{-x} & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "01b61262-b1e1-5209-b2da-3fc98cfc53df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5a9dd988-3928-5bba-9fa6-088dfac520fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9b0dc2d5-2892-5706-96b9-cbb4a702ce44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "a34cfbee-5c94-5162-9256-80942a66612e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "dfb65e36-c318-5026-b6b2-c21070996b82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4c02ff0-537c-5ba7-ae43-ff24f564feb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141112/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-141112/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-141112/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-141112/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-141112/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-141112/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141112" :question/id #uuid "8abc10be-3eb5-5e2c-9a94-244a431b287a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141112" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{y}{x},\\,y(-2)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{x} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{(-2)} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141112/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141112"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352663/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "0c4c2eb4-efdf-5a11-ae1d-d488e5cfce93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352663/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d8a6415-b53e-54f5-8a38-a2cb50262b52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352663/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-352663/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352663" :question/id #uuid "d60af566-8837-57e8-b627-8477d386c176" :question/math-academy-id "q-352663" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\,y(2)=4.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{x}^{3}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{x}^{3}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=4.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=4$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{3} \\\\ 4 & =A(2)^{3} \\\\ 4 & =A(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352663/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
